# Copy to tests/win/.env (gitignored) to test on a real Windows machine
# before a push: `make win-check`, and `make pr-check` whenever this file
# names one.
#
# The machine is a device of a Pleiades project that already manages it
# over WinRM, as the VirtualBox lab's win-check is (examples/virtualbox_lab):
# PLEIADES_WINRM_PROJECT is that project's directory (a leading ~/ is
# expanded) and PLEIADES_WINRM_DEVICE the device's name in it, the same
# two settings cmd/pleiades's WinRM release gates read. The checks use the
# credential that project holds. The machine needs go, git and tar.exe on
# its PATH (or in C:\go\bin and C:\mingit\cmd). The tests run without the
# race detector, which needs cgo and a C toolchain on Windows. A linked
# worktree with no tests/win/.env of its own reads the main worktree's.
# Delete tests/win/.env to stop testing on Windows.
PLEIADES_WINRM_PROJECT=~/pleiades-lab
PLEIADES_WINRM_DEVICE=win-check
